                "text": "The Missouri National Guard\u2019s 139th Airlift Wing's Operations Group in St. Joseph recently pulled off a legendary feat during a four-day exercise simulating a cyber-attack.\n\u201cOperations Goes Dark\u201d was successfully executed by conducting normal operations without internet, GPS, or phones. Airmen coordinated missions using hand signals, runners, smoke signals, and old-school tactics to get the job done. \nProud to see the 139th setting the bar not just for Missouri, but for the entire Department of Defense. @SecDef  @SecAFOfficial  @OfficialCSAF  @usairforce  @139AW  @AirMobilityCmd  @Missouri_NG  #warfighting #lethality #cyberwarfare #electronicwarfare",
